{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":127435,"duration_api_ms":150368,"num_turns":4,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7984fcd9-0139-4159-bb41-b151d58a890f","total_cost_usd":0.4274953499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":1045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22459,"cache_read_input_tokens":74354,"output_tokens":1112,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22459,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":137,"outputTokens":9732,"cacheReadInputTokens":961226,"cacheCreationInputTokens":57604,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2169246,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1045,"outputTokens":1112,"cacheReadInputTokens":74354,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22459,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21057075000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Both amendments are confirmed by code investigation. Amendment fr-4-0d933f53 identifies a real correctness bug where Engine::from_parts() calls refresh_habitat_registry() before step_hours validation, causing light_exposure values to be recomputed with potentially invalid parameters. When validation subsequently fails, the returned state is partially mutated, violating the contract that failed steps leave state untouched. Amendment fr-4-7dfb6287 identifies a real debuggability deficiency where check_strictly_increasing only reports the upper field name and value in its error, omitting the lower bound field name even though it is available at all three call sites.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-0d933f53","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed real bug. Engine::from_parts() at engine.rs:115 calls state.refresh_habitat_registry() which recomputes all habitat light_exposure values using the current intensity_index. In the failing test, intensity_index=1.4 causes light_exposure to be ~2x higher than the clone taken before from_parts(). When step_hours then calls enforce_invariants and validation fails (due to shrimp_assimilation_efficiency=1.2), the state has already been partially mutated via the habitat registry recomputation. This violates the documented contract that failed steps leave state untouched. Both proposed fixes (snapshot-restore or deferred recomputation) are sound."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-7dfb6287","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed valid deficiency. check_strictly_increasing at invariants.rs:399-412 takes (lower_value, upper_field, upper_value) but never the lower field name. All three call sites have the lower field name readily available (e.g., 'shrimp_params.optimal_temp_min_c') but don't pass it through. The resulting error 'invariant violation for shrimp_params.optimal_temp_max_c with value X' gives no indication of which lower bound caused the failure. Adding the lower field name to the function signature and error message is a straightforward improvement that materially aids debugging."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e9d81d3a-e8c0-4720-9c3f-761429b2bc18"}
